// Run top to bottom against a fresh in-memory service; amounts are integer minor units.
// See REQUIREMENTS.md for the startup configuration gap before using these requests.
// Repeating only the transfer is safe. Re-running all requests creates new wallets: restart the service
// or choose fresh keys, because existing keys remain bound to their original account IDs for this process.
@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8080

### Create a funded wallet
// Opening funds are external issuance; the response handler saves the UUID for subsequent requests.
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{"initialBalance": 1000}

> {% client.global.set("source", response.body.id); %}

### Create an empty wallet
// Omitted initialBalance defaults to zero; explicit null is invalid. Save the destination UUID from the response.
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{}

> {% client.global.set("destination", response.body.id); %}

### Transfer (repeat this request to see the identical original outcome)
// Both accounts change atomically. Repeat with this SAME key and body to retrieve the original result.
POST {{baseUrl}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: review-payment-1

{"fromAccountId": "{{source}}", "toAccountId": "{{destination}}", "amount": 250}

### Source balance: 750
// These are two separate account snapshots; the API does not provide a global multi-account snapshot.
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{source}}/balance

### Destination balance: 250
// The successful transfer credits 250 exactly once, even after equal-key retries.
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{destination}}/balance

### Source journal: opening funding plus transfer
// Two balanced transactions should appear: opening issuance, followed by the one posted transfer.
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{source}}/entries

### Conflicting key reuse: 409
// Changing amount under a reserved key cannot create a new command; expect HTTP 409.
POST {{baseUrl}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: review-payment-1

{"fromAccountId": "{{source}}", "toAccountId": "{{destination}}", "amount": 251}

### Insufficient funds: 422, remembered on retry
// This well-formed request reaches the ledger and reserves its rejected outcome; use a new key for a new attempt.
POST {{baseUrl}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: review-insufficient-1

{"fromAccountId": "{{source}}", "toAccountId": "{{destination}}", "amount": 10000}
